just arbitrary percentages

00:49:41.250 --> 00:49:42.070
for competency.

00:49:42.070 --> 00:49:44.210
It might even be like
a Markdown template.

00:49:44.210 --> 00:49:47.910
Actually, I think for the
resume that it was generated on.

00:49:47.910 --> 00:49:48.700
So check that out.

00:49:48.700 --> 00:49:51.480
I thought that was just a
nice way to showcase, hey,

00:49:51.480 --> 00:49:54.060
I'm competent in all these
languages to varying degrees

00:49:54.060 --> 00:49:57.480
without having a super
long, detailed section.

00:49:57.480 --> 00:49:58.750
It's a nice little graph.

00:49:58.750 --> 00:49:59.800
So those cool.

00:50:02.360 --> 00:50:05.810
Do you have to
specify the scale?

00:50:05.810 --> 00:50:07.700
This was not this
is just a visual,

00:50:07.700 --> 00:50:11.540
so I guess it depends on how,
how tight you want to be.

00:50:11.540 --> 00:50:12.770
That's how you trick people.

00:50:12.770 --> 00:50:17.523
I'm a D in my R ability and
then everything else is lower.

00:50:17.523 --> 00:50:18.440
Yeah, everything else.

00:50:18.440 --> 00:50:20.750
But if you don't label
like, they don't know.

00:50:20.750 --> 00:50:22.760
Yeah, I would say, like,
it definitely depends

00:50:22.760 --> 00:50:25.280
on their personal perception.

00:50:25.280 --> 00:50:27.240
For sure, it was a bad joke.

00:50:27.240 --> 00:50:29.930
Yeah, the rank order,
relative strength.

00:50:29.930 --> 00:50:32.540
So it's up to you
as the interviewer

00:50:32.540 --> 00:50:34.240
to determine like,
OK, what's there?

00:50:34.240 --> 00:50:35.690
100 percent?

00:50:35.690 --> 00:50:38.690
Yeah with that being said,
I'd like to point out

00:50:38.690 --> 00:50:41.570
like resume formatting, right?

00:50:41.570 --> 00:50:45.350
Some, you know, some systems
will not take part starts

00:50:45.350 --> 00:50:47.810
into the resume format, right?

00:50:47.810 --> 00:50:51.180
And a lot of times they will
get printed out on gray scale.

00:50:51.180 --> 00:50:53.300
So don't make it all
nice and colorful.

00:50:53.300 --> 00:50:55.220
Make make sure like
if you do use color,

00:50:55.220 --> 00:50:57.770
that it's going to look
nice in black and white.

00:50:57.770 --> 00:51:00.740
Some of my pointers I give to
students because some of them

00:51:00.740 --> 00:51:04.260
get really creative and
like, yes, that's wonderful.

00:51:04.260 --> 00:51:05.570
I applaud your creativity.

00:51:05.570 --> 00:51:08.180
Just make sure it looks
good in black and white, so.

00:51:11.610 --> 00:51:13.540
Yeah, the resume
is so important.

00:51:13.540 --> 00:51:18.250
Just a reminder that we have
typically 300 to 500 resumes

00:51:18.250 --> 00:51:19.130
to get through.

00:51:19.130 --> 00:51:26.352
So if you submit a novel, it's
going to just go right past it.

00:51:26.352 --> 00:51:28.310
Now, that's some other
things I say, make sure,

00:51:28.310 --> 00:51:29.900
like you build
stuff, that somebody

00:51:29.900 --> 00:51:34.190
can quickly glance at it in 30
seconds for the first review,

00:51:34.190 --> 00:51:34.790
right?

00:51:34.790 --> 00:51:36.290
And you've got their
attention, then

00:51:36.290 --> 00:51:39.380
they'll go back and look at it
a little bit more detail if they

00:51:39.380 --> 00:51:41.580
see something like
that really pops out.

00:51:41.580 --> 00:51:44.960
So I always say, like bold
those important things,

00:51:44.960 --> 00:51:46.850
you know, and make it about.

00:51:46.850 --> 00:51:51.050
Because I've had, like
students will put an order

00:51:51.050 --> 00:51:51.810
on their resume.

00:51:51.810 --> 00:51:54.295
For example, the last class
